@Charles Peterson Hayduke was not fully finished but published anyway after his death without much editing or proofreading, It is not as interesting a story but the prose is often gorgeous and/or wise. The opening comparison and contrast essay about an old desert tortoise and a bulldozer climbing the same hill is both.

A short quote for our times:
Don't let yourself become cynical. Cynicism is a cheap emotion, a craven substitute for thought and action. Cynicism corrodes the will, dulls the conscience, blunts your sense of right and wrong… Stay alert to fine distinctions: become a pessimist like me..

